auf/24251'></a><figcaption>baskauf/24251<br>Gymnocladus dioicus<br>leaf · close-up</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/kirchoff/tem2584.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/kirchoff/tem2584.jpg' alt='kirchoff/em2584'></a><figcaption>kirchoff/em2584<br>Quercus palustris<br>bark · close-up</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/kirchoff/tem2563.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/kirchoff/tem2563.jpg' alt='kirchoff/em2563'></a><figcaption>kirchoff/em2563<br>Quercus palustris<br>bark · close-up</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tsaal5-brlarge11341.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tsaal5-brlarge11341.jpg' alt='baskauf/11341'></a><figcaption>baskauf/11341<br>Sassafras albidum<br>bark · close-up</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tlibe3-lf11695.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tlibe3-lf11695.jpg' alt='baskauf/11695'></a><figcaption>baskauf/11695<br>Lindera benzoin<br>leaf · close-up</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/trhcol2lfupper-lower12583.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/trhcol2lfupper-lower12583.jpg' alt='baskauf/12583'></a><figcaption>baskauf/12583<br>Rhus copallinum<br>leaf · close-up</figcaption></figure></div></dd><dt>What it supports</dt><dd>AE: the recovered results show AE MSE on par with PCA and worse neighbour retention, for all 3 models. There is no nonlinear structure worth the extra complexity, so this line stops here (recovered result + verified linear sanity check). Axes: PC1 vs scale ρ=−0.65 and vs whole tree ρ=+0.62 (close-up leaves ↔ distant whole trees); PC2 ≈ bark ↔ whole tree; PC3 ≈ inflorescence/fruit ↔ leaf; PC4 has |ρ|&lt;0.1 with every listed label, <b>no readable meaning</b>. Axis names describe correlations, not causes.</dd></dl></section><section id=e6><h2>6. Visualisation fidelity</h2><div><span class='b v'>Verified</span></div><dl><dt>Question</dt><dd>How well do 2-D / higher-dimensional PCA views keep the neighbour structure of the full space?</dd><dt>What was actually run</dt><dd>EfficientNet, PCA fit on train (1,181) only, evaluated on val (249): 15-NN overlap within the val pool, trustworthiness, reconstruction R², linear probes (C=100, same as the existing benchmark), K=20 ARI. 2-D numbers also on all 1,641 images for comparison with the site.</dd><dt>Result</dt><dd><div class=tw><table><tr><th>d</th><th>train_explained_var</th><th>val_recon_r2</th><th>val_knn15_overlap</th><th>val_trustworthiness</th><th>probe_species_macroF1</th><th>probe_organ_macroF1</th><th>kmeans20_ARI_vs_full</th></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>0.165</td><td>0.140</td><td>0.327</td><td>0.813</td><td>0.004</td><td>0.491</td><td>0.230</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>0.345</td><td>0.324</td><td>0.582</td><td>0.937</td><td>0.027</td><td>0.605</td><td>0.489</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>0.454</td><td>0.421</td><td>0.655</td><td>0.960</td><td>0.073</td><td>0.617</td><td>0.540</td></tr><tr><td>32</td><td>0.570</td><td>0.524</td><td>0.720</td><td>0.972</td><td>0.084</td><td>0.616</td><td>0.531</td></tr><tr><td>64</td><td>0.684</td><td>0.617</td><td>0.759</td><td>0.977</td><td>0.095</td><td>0.671</td><td>0.593</td></tr><tr><td>128</td><td>0.796</td><td>0.707</td><td>0.809</td><td>0.985</td><td>0.091</td><td>0.662</td><td>0.576</td></tr><tr><td>256</td><td>0.895</td><td>0.789</td><td>0.850</td><td>0.993</td><td>0.100</td><td>0.651</td><td>0.525</td></tr><tr><td>full</td><td>1.000</td><td>1.000</td><td>1.000</td><td>1.000</td><td>0.101</td><td>0.649</td><td>1.000</td></tr></table></div><img src='results/exp6_pca_fidelity.png' alt='fidelity'></dd><dt>What it supports</dt><dd>2-D keeps only about 13% of 15 nearest neighbours (all 1,641; 33% in the val pool), K=20 ARI 0.23, so <b>structure cannot be read off 2-D plots</b>. Under the pre-set rule (15-NN ≥ 0.85 and species probe within 1 pp), <b>no d* exists</b> up to 256 (256-D gives 0.850 / 0.849, on the boundary). The organ probe saturates around 64-D. (The species probe is low on val to begin with: EfficientNet is not a species model.)</dd></dl></section><section id=e7><h2>7. Inversion: retrieve the nearest real images</h2><div><span class='b v'>Verified</span> <span class='b e'>Exploratory demo</span></div><dl><dt>Question</dt><dd>What does a cluster centroid, or a point along an axis, look like?</dd><dt>What was actually run</dt><dd>No generative model is trained. In the full embedding space, retrieve the 6 nearest real images (cosine) to: the 20 EfficientNet K=20 centroids, and the mean ± 2 SD points along PC1 / PC2 (re-normalised).</dd><dt>Result</dt><dd><div class=tw><table><tr><th>point</th><th>cluster_size</th><th>cluster_dominant_organ</th><th>cluster_dominant_share</th><th>top1_cos</th><th>top6_in_cluster</th><th>top6_share_dominant_organ</th><th>top6_n_species</th></tr><tr><td>centroid c0</td><td>136.00</td><td>inflorescence</td><td>0.49</td><td>0.71</td><td>6.00</td><td>0.67</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>centroid c1</td><td>92.00</td><td>whole tree</td><td>0.40</td><td>0.78</td><td>6.00</td><td>0.83</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>centroid c2</td><td>126.00</td><td>leaf</td><td>0.74</td><td>0.85</td><td>6.00</td><td>0.83</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>centroid c3</td><td>65.00</td><td>whole tree</td><td>1.00</td><td>0.84</td><td>5.00</td><td>1.00</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>centroid c4</td><td>69.00</td><td>whole tree</td><td>0.77</td><td>0.85</td><td>6.00</td><td>0.67</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>centroid c5</td><td>86.00</td><td>bark</td><td>1.00</td><td>0.93</td><td>6.00</td><td>1.00</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>centroid c6</td><td>122.00</td><td>inflorescence</td><td>0.70</td><td>0.78</td><td>6.00</td><td>1.00</t