orescence · distant · cos 0.80</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tulam--flin-flower10343.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tulam--flin-flower10343.jpg' alt='baskauf/10343'></a><figcaption>baskauf/10343<br>Ulmus americana<br>inflorescence · mid-range · cos 0.80</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tacru--wpin-flower50750.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tacru--wpin-flower50750.jpg' alt='baskauf/50750'></a><figcaption>baskauf/50750<br>Acer rubrum<br>whole tree · distant · cos 0.78</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tacru--fldistant00000.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tacru--fldistant00000.jpg' alt='baskauf/00000'></a><figcaption>baskauf/00000<br>Acer rubrum<br>inflorescence · distant · cos 0.78</figcaption></figure></div><h4>PC1 -2SD</h4><div class=strip><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tzaam--lfpetiole-lower35728.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tzaam--lfpetiole-lower35728.jpg' alt='baskauf/35728'></a><figcaption>baskauf/35728<br>Zanthoxylum americanum<br>leaf · close-up · cos 0.76</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tploc--tw15360.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tploc--tw15360.jpg' alt='baskauf/15360'></a><figcaption>baskauf/15360<br>Platanus occidentalis<br>twig · mid-range · cos 0.73</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tqubi--lf12366.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tqubi--lf12366.jpg' alt='baskauf/12366'></a><figcaption>baskauf/12366<br>Quercus bicolor<br>leaf · close-up · cos 0.73</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tacru--lf11920.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tacru--lf11920.jpg' alt='baskauf/11920'></a><figcaption>baskauf/11920<br>Acer rubrum<br>leaf · close-up · cos 0.72</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tfram2-lf12465.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tfram2-lf12465.jpg' alt='baskauf/12465'></a><figcaption>baskauf/12465<br>Fraxinus americana<br>leaf · close-up · cos 0.72</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tcaca18lfbase15696.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tcaca18lfbase15696.jpg' alt='baskauf/15696'></a><figcaption>baskauf/15696<br>Carpinus caroliniana<br>leaf · close-up · cos 0.71</figcaption></figure></div><h4>PC1 +2SD</h4><div class=strip><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tprse2-flin-flower10643.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tprse2-flin-flower10643.jpg' alt='baskauf/10643'></a><figcaption>baskauf/10643<br>Prunus serotina<br>whole tree · distant · cos 0.77</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/t89397.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/t89397.jpg' alt='baskauf/89397'></a><figcaption>baskauf/89397<br>Pinus strobus<br>whole tree · distant · cos 0.77</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/t91107.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/t91107.jpg' alt='baskauf/91107'></a><figcaption>baskauf/91107<br>Ulmus americana<br>whole tree · distant · cos 0.76</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tquma2-wplarge12413.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/tquma2-wplarge12413.jpg' alt='baskauf/12413'></a><figcaption>baskauf/12413<br>Quercus macrocarpa<br>whole tree · distant · cos 0.76</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/t91011.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/t91011.jpg' alt='baskauf/91011'></a><figcaption>baskauf/91011<br>Acer rubrum<br>whole tree · distant · cos 0.75</figcaption></figure><figure><a href='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/t90911.jpg' target=_blank><img loading=lazy src='https://bioimages.vanderbilt.edu/tn/baskauf/t90911.jpg' alt='baskauf/90911'></a><figcaption>baskauf/90911<br>Platanus occidentalis<br>whole tree · distant · cos 0.74</figcaption></figure></div></dd><dt>What it supports</dt><dd>On average 6.0/6 neighbours of a centroid belong to that cluster, and 90% show its dominant organ vs 82% across the whole cluster. Retrieval returns the cluster's typical members, which overstates cluster purity when shown. PC1 −2SD → close-up leaves, +2SD → distant whole trees, consistent with item 5. This is retrieval, not image generation.</dd></dl></section><section id=e8><h2>Appendix: the same vector-only experiments on BioCLIP 2.5 and DINOv3</h2><div><span class='b v'>Verified</span></div><p>Raw BioCLIP 2.5 (1,641 × 1,024) and DINOv3 (1,641 × 768) vectors were recovered from Drive after the main run. SHA-256 recorded, image_id order and splits checked against the manifest. Items 1, 4, 5, 6 and 7 were rerun unchanged with <code>FGV_MODEL=bioclip|dinov3</code> (outputs in results/bioclip/, results/dinov3/). Item 3 still needs the BioCLIP / DINOv3 model weights. The NSC grouping task and retrieval use each model's own existing K=20 clusters. Entropy-vs-error AUROC is EfficientNet-only (per-image predictions of the other models are not in Git).</p><div class=tw><table><tr><th>model</th><th>2D 15-NN (all 1,641)</th><th>64D 15-NN (val)</th><th>d*</th><th>species probe F1 (val, full)</th><th>organ probe F1 (val, full)</th><th>NSC organ coords @1-SE</th><th>NSC organ F1 1-SE/Δ0</th><th>GMM max&lt;0.6</th><th>GMM seed ARI</th><th>entropy AUROC mid-range</th><th>PC1 ρ scale</th><th>PCA-32 test MSE (site)</th><th>linear AE / PCA</th><th>centroid top-6 dominant organ</th></tr><tr><td>BioCLIP 2.5</td><td>0.096</td><td>0.746</td><td>256</td><td>0.791</td><td>0.725</td><td>64</td><td>0.977</td><td>0.011</td><td>0.556</td><td>0.373</td><td>0.033</td><td>0.000284 (0.000284)</td><td>1.000</td><td>0.500</td></tr><tr><td>DINOv3</td><td>0.143</td><td>0.806</td><td>&gt;256</td><td>0.431</td><td>0.828</td><td>64</td><td>0.958</td><td>0.008</td><td>0.566</td><td>0.619</td><td>-0.506</td><td>0.000498 (0.000498)</td><td>1.000</td><td>0.908</td></tr><tr><td>EfficientNet-B0</td><td>0.125</td><td>0.759</td><td>&gt;256</td><td>0.101</td><td>0.649</td><td>22</td><td>0.971</td><td>0.013</td><td>0.657</td><td>0.639</td><td>-0.645</td><td>0.000296 (0.000296)</td><td>1.003</td><td>0.900</td></tr></table></div><h4>BioCLIP 2.5: PC1–3</h4><div class=tw><table><tr><th>pc</th><th>var</th><th>rho_scale_close</th><th>rho_brightness</th><th>reading</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>0.09</td><td>0.03</td><td>-0.00</td><td>no clear organ correlate (all |rho|&lt;0.2)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>0.05</td><td>0.12</td><td>-0.05</td><td>no clear organ correlate (all |rho|&lt;0.2)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>0.04</td><td>-0.45</td><td>0.34</td><td>low end ~ leaf, high end ~ whole tree</td></tr></table></div><h4>DINOv3: PC1–3</h4><div class=tw><table><tr><th>pc</th><th>var</th><th>rho_scale_close</th><th>rho_brightness</th><th>reading</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>0.09</td><td>-0.51</td><td>0.33</td><td>low end ~ leaf, high end ~ whole tree</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>0.06</td><td>-0.59</td><td>0.18</td><td>low end ~ bark, high end ~ whole tree</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>0.05</td><td>0.00</td><td>-0.10</td><td>low end ~ leaf, high end ~ inflorescence</td></tr></table></div><h4>EfficientNet-B0: PC1–3</h4><div class=tw><table><tr><th>pc</th><th>var</th><th>rho_scale_close</th><th>rho_brightness</th><th>reading</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>0.10</td><td>-0.65</td><td>0.33</td><td>low end ~ leaf, high end ~ whole tree</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>0.06</td><td>-0.44</td><td>0.11</td><td>low end ~ bark, high end ~ whole tree</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>0.05</td><td>-0.04</td><td>0.14</td><td>low end ~ inflorescence, high end ~ leaf</td></tr></table></div><p>Reading: (1) The recovered vectors are the ones used before: PCA-32 test MSE reproduces the hosted AE table to 6 decimals for all three models, and the linear AE matches PCA (ratio ≈ 1). (2) 2-D keeps 10–14% of 15 nearest neighbours for every model; only BioCLIP reaches the d* rule, at 256-D. (3) The shot-scale axis is PC1 in EfficientNet (ρ=−0.65) and DINOv3 (ρ=−0.51) but only PC3 in BioCLIP (ρ=−0.45; PC1–2 |ρ|≤0.12), consistent with BioCLIP being species-first. (4) NSC sparsifies the organ task only in EfficientNet (22/64 coordinates); in BioCLIP and DINOv3 organ information stays spread over all 64 components. (5) Soft GMM membership is near-hard for all three (≤1.3% images with max membership &lt;0.6). (6) Retrieved centroid neighbours show the cluster's dominant organ 90–91% of the time for DINOv3 / EfficientNet but 50% for BioCLIP, whose clusters are not organ clusters. Single split, single seed per setting; descriptive where noted.</p></section><section><h2>Reproduce</h2><pre>cd botanical-computer-vision/meeting_minimal
 bash fetch_images.sh          # 1,641 originals + thumbnails -> /home/user/imgcache (not committed)
 bash run_all.sh               # exp1–exp7 on EfficientNet
 bash run_models.sh            # vector-only items on BioCLIP / DINOv3, then rebuild both reports</pre>
